9	 * clock, pinmux, register, and interrupt handling while the NuttX serial
10	 * upper half owns the RX and TX ring buffers.  The SDK software RX FIFO is
11	 * disabled so its ISR leaves received bytes in the hardware FIFO before
12	 * invoking bk7258_uart_sdk_isr().
13	 *
14	 * TX remains synchronously polled through bk_uart_write_bytes().  Early boot
15	 * output remains available through bk7258_lowputc.c; the full SDK UART setup
16	 * is deferred to arm_serialinit(), after NuttX memory and semaphore services
17	 * are available.  CONFIG_BK7258_SDK_IRQ_BRIDGE provides the SDK-to-NuttX IRQ
18	 * registration path used by bk_uart_init().
19	 ****************************************************************************/
20	
